1
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:04,719
So… what actually happens to your brain

2
00:00:04,739 --> 00:00:06,078
when you get a concussion?

3
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:10,311
A concussion is a type of brain injury

4
00:00:10,331 --> 00:00:12,743
caused by a bump, blow, or jolt to the

5
00:00:12,763 --> 00:00:15,430
head— or even a hit to the body that makes

6
00:00:15,450 --> 00:00:17,989
the brain move rapidly inside the skull.

7
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:23,133
Even when there's no obvious damage on a

8
00:00:23,153 --> 00:00:25,813
scan, that sudden movement can temporarily

9
00:00:25,833 --> 00:00:28,302
disrupt how brain cells communicate and

10
00:00:28,322 --> 00:00:29,961
how the brain uses energy.

11
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:36,142
That can lead to symptoms like headache,

12
00:00:36,162 --> 00:00:38,063
dizziness, fatigue, brain fog,

13
00:00:38,083 --> 00:00:40,561
trouble concentrating, memory problems,

14
00:00:40,581 --> 00:00:42,738
or sensitivity to light and noise.

15
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:48,081
And here's something important:

16
00:00:48,101 --> 00:00:50,404
you do not have to lose consciousness to

17
00:00:50,424 --> 00:00:51,972
have a concussion. In fact,

18
00:00:51,992 --> 00:00:54,063
most people with concussions do not.

19
00:00:57,400 --> 00:00:59,739
Symptoms can also show up right away—

20
00:00:59,759 --> 00:01:02,034
or develop hours or even days later.

21
00:01:02,054 --> 00:01:04,711
That's why it's important to pay attention

22
00:01:04,731 --> 00:01:07,134
to how you're feeling after an injury.

23
00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:11,404
If you think you've had a concussion,

24
00:01:11,424 --> 00:01:13,701
stop the activity and get evaluated by a

25
00:01:13,721 --> 00:01:15,021
qualified professional.

26
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:17,825
A concussion is a brain injury.

27
00:01:17,845 --> 00:01:20,028
I'm your brain— let's learn together.

